roland emerick has been doing some  interviews and he's been asked directly  about stargate what he had to say is  very very interesting  welcome to sidetrack your sci-fi tv a  movie channel  so roland emrick's new movie moon 4 is  out at cinemas and to be fair it's not  done very well more importantly he's  been asked directly about the stargaze  series and his answers have actually  reinforced a lot of what i've been  saying over the last few months about  the return of stargate to our tv screens  so first of all he was basically  directly asked are you going to return  to do a stargate movie because he has  been lined up to do one before his  answer was  it's not going to happen  the reason why it's not going to happen  though is very telling he said i thought  that the people that watched the tv show  are the main focus that's a really  interesting point because i did a video  a little while ago about mgm we're  really considering three main options  for stargate plan a is a movie followed  by a tv series  plan b if the sale of mgm to amazon  drags on much longer they will start  with a tv series and then follow up with  a movie this is basically down to how  long it takes a movie to be produced and  how long it takes a tv show to be  produced obviously a tv show is much  quicker and they really have a deadline  that they wanted something on the  screens by and the end of 2023 so if the  sale drags on a long time they're going  to want to start with the tv series  because they can get on our screens  faster than the canon movie they want  the movie first ideally because they  really want to build a lot of hype up  plan c  was to actually do a hard reboot now  roland emmerich and dean devlin many  years ago this actually when the first  stargate movie came out always planned  that movie to be a trilogy but it got  turned into the tv series eventually now  he actually says in this interview that  he was offered to do the tv series  himself he actually did look into it but  he said everything he does has a certain  production value and basically the  amount of money they were offering pers  tvs episode the budget was only about  eight hundred thousand dollars at a time  when the x-files was getting made for  over a million dollars an episode so he  basically felt it's not going to be  enough money i don't want to do  something that is half-hearted so he  decided not to do the sg-1 series but  his point about the fans of the tv show  being the focus for producers really is  internet again underlies what i've been  saying for a few months  that they do not want to do a hard  reboot of this series they want to do a  soft reboot a continuation of the story  this really does confirm now that plan c  is out of the window we will not be  getting a hard reboot of stargate we  will only be getting a soft reboot and a  continuation of the sg-1 sg universe and  sg atlantis series now i did actually  tell you in a video a few months ago the  role of denmark was actually in meetings  with mgm and amazon executives in  november apparently the existing plan  for the trilogy was pitched once again  to those people  and they were seriously considering  doing this actually having a full hard  reboot i've done a video actually  talking about why they thought about  that because you know it is a lot easier  to do a hard reboot in lots of ways  you've got a lot of canon you don't need  to worry about too much so  in some ways it's better but it's not  what we want and amazon i know it's not  what we want as fans but what roland  emerick here is saying it basically  confirms that those meetings actually  did happen  now  i don't know exactly what happened in  those meetings my source at mgm who told  me about this just is aware that they  did happen but from what ronald emmerich  here is saying it looks like these were  early discussions they were sort of  putting the idea out there roland rick  said what he would want and amazon  basically said no  but there is another reason why those  meetings happened it turns out the role  of limerick is still actually contracted  to mgm and stargate he actually says  that if there is a movie or a series of  movies produced that he will have to be  involved in some way because he's  contracted to do so now obviously mgm  could not trigger that contract they  could decide not to but if they want  roland emerick to be involved in some  way he will be now even though he says  he is not going to be involved directly  in the movie in in a directing or  writing approach and he will have to be  involved in some way but but not as much  as he won't be show running it he does  actually go on to say that he really  hopes they will make a movie on a series  of movies i think he's actually saying  this because he knows that's the plan  from the meetings he would have had with  mgm mans and he knows that the plan is  to produce a new movie  when that movie comes out is gonna very  much dependent on the sale like i say  but roland emerick is kind of if you  read between the lines confirming that  actually that is the plan and that is  something that they are seriously  considering so to wrap that up in a nice  little bow  wrong denrick is basically confirmed to  us if you read between the lines that a  movie is at least being considered  he's also confirmed to us that these  meetings did happen um towards the end  of november like i reported previously  but most importantly he has confirmed  that for mgm and amazon the tv audience  the tv fans the fans of sg-1 and sg  atlantis st universe are their main  focus  so for me that basically underlines and  means that plan c is  completely out of the window we will not  be getting a hard reboot of stargate and  all i can say to that is  hallelujah one last thing roland rick  actually did say in this interview with  space.com though is that he's not  actually considering doing any more  science fiction novels except maybe one  the forever war has been in  pre-production for a very long time um  channing tatum was actually signed on to  do this movie got seven years ago but it  never happened ronaldo has said that is  the only science fiction novel that he  would be interested in  so very possibly we might be getting a  forever war movie or maybe even a tv  series at some point in the future if  roland emerick gets his way i haven't  actually seen moonfall yet but i love a  lot of roland and rick's previous work  he's a bit hit and miss for me but as a  filmmaker he's great and i think  actually with a source material  something like the forever war he could  create something great  so  get into the comments tell me what you  think am i reading a bit too much into  this interview perhaps or do you think  that actually yeah roland is confirming  a lot of what i've been saying for the  last few months and if you are new to  the channel please like subscribe hit  that bell notification it really helps  us out you can also join the channel and  become a fully fledged side tracker hit  the join button  as always guys please stay safe i'll see

